WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.570
It's gotta be leather.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:09.760
If it's thread, it won't 
dry when it's wet.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.530
Hey, that's not right.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.750
You relax the knees.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.200
It's faster that way.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:19.570
Here.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:21.060
Thank you.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.080
Sensei, someone named Morse 
wants to interview you.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:27.170
What's an interview?

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.300
A documentary.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.800
I'd like your help with a TV special.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.260
A TV camera!

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:40.010
So I can be on TV?

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:20.300
Nobody knows where the 
Samurai came from,

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.820
but now they're living in our world.

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:24.920
They insist they didn't come

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:27.920
to the modern world of their own will.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:32.080
Well, whatever the reason, 
they're strangers here.

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:33.870
Since they're not 
registered as citizens,

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.780
the poor girls can't even receive

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:38.590
the basic services we take for granted.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.100
Many of them are unable 
to adapt to modern life,

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:46.680
and are in poverty and 
unhappily, we're told.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.060
But is that true?

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:51.560
The Samurai are popular all over Japan!

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:53.940
Some of them are even idols!

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:58.050
It's possible that instead 
of taking pity on them,

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:00.590
we should envy them.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.510
Of course, that's impossible right?

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:09.570
No, no, they seem to have 
different rights than we do.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:16.550
For example: are they allowed 
the right to carry swords?

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:20.240
This is a recreation. 
The case has not been solved.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:24.390
This is footage of a cruel murder.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:26.670
According to later reports,

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:29.050
the suspect left home 
after seeing a rerun

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:30.440
of a Samurai TV show.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:34.100
Was that what brought it on?

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:37.230
Yes, he wanted to be a Samurai.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:55.290
Are you really the sensei 
here at the dojo?

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:56.690
Yup.

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.340
That's amazing, as little as you are.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:59.540
Is it?

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:00.260
Are you strong?

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.400
Super strong!

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.260
Seriously?

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:05.540
Once I've got a katana in my hand,
 I won't lose to anybody.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:08.140
<b>Ento Sword Shop</b>

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.460
Hello.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:10.690
Welcome.

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:12.940
There're lots of swords here.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.180
Well, it's a sword shop.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.030
Do you sell to anybody?

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:17.760
That's right.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.710
Anybody can have one if 
they have permission.

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:21.370
I can buy one?

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:23.150
If you've got the money.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:28.490
As you can see, it's easy 
to get a katana here.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.670
We've got a home video here.

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.110
You can do it!

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.540
I did it! I did it!

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:45.490
It's hard to believe,

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:48.830
but this is the girl from 
the dojo, earlier.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:51.270
The mother taking the video 
was unable to do anything.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.100
What incredible cruelty!

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.320
Bokuden-chan is very serious when

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.360
it comes to swordsmanship.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.930
It's hard to imagine 
from looking at her.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:06.850
She's a kid, isn't she?

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.540
But isn't it dangerous 
for a child to change

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:12.080
that drastically when she has a katana?

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.680
Possibly.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:18.130
But I've never heard of 
her hurting anybody.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.140
Do you know what kind 
of personality she has?

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:22.490
I do.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:23.640
She just pretends to be cute.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.100
I don't like her at all.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.030
She's nastier than you'd think.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:28.880
You mean her personality is bad?

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:32.140
Yeah. I guess that's how you'd say it.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.950
So she's a bad child.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.020
Yeah.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.560
Like that dojo.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.100
She calls it "Katsujinken," 
but that's something I invented.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:41.480
"Katsujinken"?

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:45.030
A style whose goal is improving 
yourself, not killing people.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:47.280
So you just hurt them really 
badly instead of killing them?

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.870
Of course not.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.280
But it's possible that 
that's what Bokuden

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.910
means when she uses the word.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:56.540
So her personality is 
dangerous, in other words.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:57.750
Yeah.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.540
You can't let your 
guard down around her.

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:03.530
Some say you can't let your 
guard down around her.

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:05.400
That's right.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.110
She is a swordsman.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:09.510
All swordsmen are dangerous, right?

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.050
Not at all.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.270
Just sometimes some of 
them are dangerous.

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:14.650
What do you mean?

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:16.810
They wouldn't attack someone 
randomly, would they?

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.500
No. They fight each other.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:24.320
Sometimes they want to 
test each other's skills.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.500
Have you ever fought Bokuden?

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:28.430
Yeah, we've had lots of little matches.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:29.530
With real swords?

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:30.710
Never.

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:32.500
That's why I made things like

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.280
wooden swords and defensive gear.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:37.350
But that's basically practice, right?

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:41.830
Yeah. We've had real fights.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.800
When you say "dangerous..."

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:46.920
I suppose the girl named Itou 
Ittousai is a little dangerous.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.780
She's a wandering swordsman 
who likes using real swords.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:51.800
Bokuden's fought her.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:53.710
Lots of times, I think.

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:57.910
Ittousai will go after anybody 
who people say is strong.

00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.410
Like a mad bull.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:02.440
Isn't it dangerous for them 
to fight in the streets?

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.860
Yes.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:07.450
So you Samurai generals 
are dangerous, then?

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:11.100
Dangerous, but we know our limits.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:13.820
And we're only interested in the strong.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:17.490
I've never heard of anyone 
hurting a normal person.

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:19.820
Even so, they are causing others

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:23.790
to take an interest in swordplay, right?

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:29.380
That's something I do feel 
responsible for as a Shogun.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:34.620
In this light, don't the Samurai 
feel extremely dangerous?

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:38.130
In fact, while there have been 
multiple cases of murders

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:41.420
Murders influenced by

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:41.420
Samurai Generals

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:41.420
Japan

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:41.420
overseas

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:40.050
influenced by the Samurai in Japan,

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:41.440
there have been none over seas.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.690
But the Samurai are very popular with kids.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.380
Dangerous weapons,

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:50.690
dangerous people, are being 
left to roam the streets.

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:54.950
But everyone seems to accept them.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.950
What is behind this odd turn of events?

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:03.620
To understand, let's take 
a look at Japan's history.

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:07.710
Hey, boys and girls, 
it's time for history class!

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:11.220
Japan has always loved war.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.640
In the feudal period especially,

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.430
they killed each other all over Japan!

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.420
In other words, those lords and generals

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:18.390
loved killing each other!

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:22.430
But Japan has always 
viewed them as heroes.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.440
Corporate leaders compare 
themselves to them,

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.940
and housewives love watching 
TV shows about them!

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:33.830
That's right, Japan loves 
those Samurai generals!

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:39.030
And that means the Japanese 
still love killing each other!

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:45.000
Swords are for killing people.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.430
Why do you teach people to use them?

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:49.610
It's important to be able to kill.

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.450
What does that mean?

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:53.960
People die surprisingly easily.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:56.370
Whether you can do it 
or not is important.

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:58.100
You like killing people.

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:02.760
My students don't seem to, 
so they avoid practice.

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:05.010
But I love it!

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:11.540
No, that's not what I said!

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.770
It's a simple interview.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:20.880
Interview?

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:23.620
Yes, you can just answer some questions.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:24.700
Sure!

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:25.870
Ask whatever you want!

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.700
I'm Bokuden-chan, 
the bodhisattva swordsman!

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.380
My favorite food is chocolate!

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:34.200
Um, those will be our last questions.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.130
I want to hear about sword fighting.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:39.230
You teach that, right?

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:40.140
Yup.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:42.680
Swords are for killing people.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.460
Why do you teach people to use them?

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:46.230
It sounds strange,

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.720
but it's because it keeps 
you from having to kill.

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:50.020
But swords are for killing.

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:53.940
It's important to be 
able to kill a person.

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:56.830
Because if you can, you don't have to.

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:58.450
What does that mean?

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:01.150
People die surprisingly easily.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:05.250
If you know that, you don't 
take your weapon up so easily.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:08.000
But you have a sword.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.730
Whether you can do it 
or not is important.

00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:14.000
If you can't, you can't protect anyone.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:17.120
The more things you can do, 
the stronger you are, right?

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:18.970
So the stronger wins?

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.850
Nope.

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:22.720
In the end, you don't use your weapon and

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.220
you win without hurting anyone.

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:26.330
So you don't like killing people.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:27.700
Of course!

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:29.820
But you like sword fighting.

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:34.190
My students don't seem to, 
so they avoid practice.

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:36.820
But to me, that's life!

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.340
Bokuden-chan, do you like chocolate?

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:41.530
I love it!

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:43.820
Are you really the teacher at this dojo?

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:44.930
Yup.

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:49.700
So this whole thing is a lie?

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:52.280
I spent two hours talking to him!

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:56.550
All the parts where I 
advertised my dojo are gone!

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:58.510
<b>Morse's Office</b>

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:02.020
Hello. Yes, hello there.

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:03.800
Super popular?

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:06.310
Thank you!

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:07.260
Thanks.

00:11:08.550 --> 00:11:09.950
Hello, hello...

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:11.530
A part two?

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:12.970
That sounds great.

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:14.590
I'll get started.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:19.320
Do it at the studio, 
with live broadcast parts?

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:22.570
Yes. I'll do it, of course. Yes.

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:26.910
It worked!

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:41.040
Mom says I can't play 
with you, Bokuden-chan.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:42.790
She says we can't have 
any more sword fights.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:43.810
Let's go!

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:47.220
Hey.

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:49.780
It's an old woman.

00:11:49.780 --> 00:11:51.350
I'm not old.

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:53.790
You piss me off every time I see you.

00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:55.760
Oh well, forget it.

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:58.230
This time it looks like you're 
having a hard time, too.

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:00.240
Because of that TV program.

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:02.610
Of course.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.210
I got fired from my job at school.

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:08.080
See? Everybody's talking about it.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:07.060
<b>Danger!! 
Samurai 
Generals</b>

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:08.080
<b>Deadly weapon</b>

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.250
That TV show was all lies.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.500
I didn't say any of that stuff!

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:13.850
That's right.

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:15.430
They edited it,

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:17.820
to make it the opposite of
 what I actually said.

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:21.630
Everybody's gonna stop 
coming to my dojo!

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:23.660
My first impulse is to beat the

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:25.500
crap out of the guy who made the video,

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:30.440
but that would just 
prove we're dangerous.

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:36.400
Our next special program 
will include live footage.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:38.090
Live footage?

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.360
They don't record it.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:42.400
They just broadcast everything 
that's said immediately.

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:45.590
If only we were on a live broadcast,

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:47.350
we could've told the truth.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:49.200
Then let's go!

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.660
It's not gonna work.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:52.220
They won't let us in,

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:55.210
and if we fight our way in, 
that's just what they want.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:58.060
If people saw that happening 
on live broadcast

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:00.340
that would be the end.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:04.090
I know!

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:05.880
<b>Morse's Office</b>

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:07.540
Yes? Who's there?

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:10.810
Let me see Morse.

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:13.100
Please, let me see Morse!

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:14.960
Are you okay?

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:19.360
Jeez... Okay, I can't let you in, but...

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.900
I'll buy you a drink.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:23.690
Morse is gone?

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:27.210
Sorry. Nobody's in the office.

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:30.580
So I know what you want to 
say, but it's impossible.

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:34.000
Hey, what are you doing 
on the live broadcast?

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:36.740
Are you gonna be mean 
to Bokuden there, too?

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:39.850
No, well...

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:42.440
We're gonna have Ashikaga 
Yoshiteru-san come

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:44.230
to the studio and have her apologize to

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:47.140
the kid who got hurt by a Samurai.

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:48.520
Is that a lie, too?

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:50.560
It's not a lie, but...

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:54.350
We've talked to Ashikaga Yoshiteru-san.

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:57.520
We're recording it today.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:59.780
So we aren't lying.

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:05.460
We'll both talk, 
and Yoshiteru-san will apologize.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.400
Then am I okay?

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:10.870
Can I play with my friends?

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:13.320
It's okay.

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:16.120
Once it's all over, 
everything will be settled.

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:18.070
Okay, got it.

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:19.450
Okay, then.

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:22.470
I'm going home.

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:34.310
It worked.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:35.320
Nice.

00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:37.200
I guess you get smart when you get old.

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:39.040
I'm not that old.

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:40.940
We can fight now if you want.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:44.270
Now, now... 
I have to do this fight first.

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:44.270
<b>Challenge to a Duel</b>

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.940
You're really calling that nutjob?

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:49.030
Yup. I've got an idea.

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:51.880
And we have another ace up our sleeve.

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:54.440
If Yoshiteru-chan is busy 
on the live broadcast,

00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:56.040
that makes things easier.

00:14:56.760 --> 00:15:00.170
The danger of the Samurai is clear!

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:05.670
They carry weapons and teach 
other people how to use them.

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:08.670
And of course, they themselves 
use those weapons

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:11.180
to badly injure people.

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:14.430
What should we do about this?

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:15.930
<b>Another random 
attack committed 
in broad daylight.</b>

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:18.180
The attacker studied Kendo 
at his high school.

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:21.690
Of course, that was obviously 
the reason for the attack.

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.190
He used a blade.

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:27.190
That's right, a blade, 
just like how a katana has a blade!

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.190
The Samurai caused this.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.200
So shouldn't the Samurai apologize to

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.730
the victim and put aside their swords?

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:43.870
Fifteen minutes. That's all.

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:45.450
That's enough.

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:46.670
We just want one thing.

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:49.130
Your apology to this child.

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:52.010
With you representing 
all the other Samurai.

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:55.420
I'm not representing them.

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:58.890
Even so, your apology 
will be the beginning.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:00.970
Don't you think?

00:16:00.970 --> 00:16:03.150
Who is that child, anyway?

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:07.200
The child who was injured 
in the attack yesterday.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:09.260
The attacker was influenced 
by the Samurai

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:10.840
and carried a blade.

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:11.940
A katana?

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:13.400
Likely.

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:17.240
I don't think that's my fault.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:20.450
Possibly, but this problem 
involves the Samurai.

00:16:20.940 --> 00:16:23.450
It may be a problem for all humanity.

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:26.130
Whisper whisper.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:27.960
It's time.

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:29.040
Goodbye.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:31.760
You can't even apologize?

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:34.510
Let me know if you ever 
change your mind.

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:37.010
I'll be waiting.

00:16:40.010 --> 00:16:41.850
Now then, we're waiting for

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:44.520
word from Ashikaga Yoshiteru-san 
during our broadcast.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:47.520
If you want to apologize here,

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:51.110
then, Yoshiteru-san, come to the studio.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:52.910
This is the child who can

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:54.860
no longer walk because of the attack.

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:57.790
Yoshiteru-san, if you have 
any shred of compassion...

00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:58.870
One second!

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:01.500
We've got word from Yoshiteru-san!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.460
She'll be coming to the studio

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:05.170
with a special recorded segment!

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:11.320
What a moving moment!

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:13.380
Thank you for coming, Yoshiteru-san!

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:15.330
You've decided to apologize?

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:17.850
I've considered many things.

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:19.890
Is he the child?

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:28.640
Does that mean you'll 
abandon your sword?

00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:29.740
Yes.

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:31.270
As a representative of all the Samurai,

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:33.820
I promise to put away our swords.

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:37.300
A historic moment!

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:38.990
The Samurai have put away their swords!

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:41.560
This is the beginning of a new era!

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:46.250
Let's take a look at the 
video she's brought.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:48.800
It contains a recording of 
them abandoning their weapons

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:52.000
and the process that led to 
her deciding to apologize.

00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:56.500
We would like to publicly 
state that the contents

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:59.660
of "Samurai For Murder" 
are a complete fabrication.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:01.970
Especially that video of my child being

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:04.030
attacked by Bokuden-chan,
 it was a total lie!

00:18:04.030 --> 00:18:07.560
Bokuden-chan protected my child!

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:08.690
It's true!

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.690
There were lots of bees and 
they were about to sting me,

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:12.360
and then she protected me!

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:15.860
That part wasn't used in the broadcast.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:18.360
I was so scared!

00:18:21.110 --> 00:18:21.990
Impossible!

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:23.400
That's fake!

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:26.480
I made sure there were 
no copies of that video

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:28.260
and saved it in my office!

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:30.630
There's no way you could have it!

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:33.420
So you just admitted it, Morse!

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:35.960
Bokuden!

00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:38.190
How?

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:39.720
Then this video...

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:42.220
Yup. I borrowed it.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:45.160
Sekishusai did, actually.

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:46.560
Then...

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:48.260
That's right.

00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:50.220
Oh, I don't think I mentioned this.

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:52.900
I'm Shogun, but I'm also 
one of Bokuden's students.

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:54.070
You were conspiring against me?

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:56.370
That's not a nice way to put it.

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:58.740
I just exchanged that video with the

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:02.180
one we planned to broadcast here.

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:06.620
If anyone's conspiring here, 
it would be you and I:

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:08.370
we planned this meeting in advance.

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:10.670
What a tremendous event!

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:12.670
Morse's hugely popular documentary

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:14.630
has been accused of being a fraud!

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:16.120
This is defamation of character!

00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:17.380
A fraud?

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:19.640
And even if it was a fraud,

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:21.890
I proved how dangerous the Samurai are!

00:19:22.230 --> 00:19:25.220
They stole that data from my office!

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:27.170
The Samurai are dangerous!

00:19:27.170 --> 00:19:28.500
Katanas are dangerous!

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:31.810
This was just a dramatization 
to make that point!

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:34.610
Sure, they're dangerous.

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:37.820
But one of those dangerous Samurai 
is on her way here right now.

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:43.120
I am Ittousai.

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:45.910
Who calls themselves the strongest?

00:19:48.310 --> 00:19:50.440
Bokuden! You're kidding me!

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:51.960
You're supposed to be the strongest!

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:55.880
Nope. I lost to Morse 
and threw away my sword.

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:59.630
Shut up. He doesn't even have a sword.

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:00.960
He has a camera.

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:03.090
A camera is stronger than a sword.

00:20:04.030 --> 00:20:05.260
A camera, huh?

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:06.770
That's an impressive weapon.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:09.290
Let us fight!

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:11.140
I am Ittousai!

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:17.650
Didn't you Samurai throw away your weapons?

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:19.310
It doesn't matter what Yoshiteru says!

00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:20.860
Who'd listen to her?

00:20:26.270 --> 00:20:28.200
You won't get away!

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:31.870
Save me!

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:33.040
I'm sorry!

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:34.940
I'm sorry I tricked you!

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:36.290
So save me!

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:37.440
Can't help.

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:39.340
I threw away my sword.

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:40.240
I get it!

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:41.510
I get it now!

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:43.140
There are things you can't protect

00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:44.650
if you throw away your sword!

00:20:44.650 --> 00:20:45.590
So...

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:47.950
Bokuden doesn't lie.

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:50.140
So I don't have a sword now.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:53.150
I was wrong! I was very wrong!

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:54.550
Swords are necessary!

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:55.590
We need swords!

00:20:55.590 --> 00:20:56.770
So you apologize?

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:57.590
I apologize.

00:20:57.590 --> 00:20:58.520
I'm sorry!

00:20:58.520 --> 00:20:59.400
I'm sorry.

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:01.250
Then I'll forgive you.

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:05.380
But that's not your mistake.

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:06.960
Your gravestone will say

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:10.040
"I was killed by the 
strongest swordsman!"

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:12.540
I am Ittousai!

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:19.160
You made one mistake.

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:22.050
Both blades and cameras are weapons.

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:24.770
You blocked me with that thing?

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:28.100
This is the biggest 
humiliation of my life...

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:30.350
Impressive, master.

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:34.520
Aww, I guess I'm the strongest again.

00:21:39.390 --> 00:21:41.020
I did it!

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:45.430
He's back!

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:46.770
What do you want?

00:21:46.770 --> 00:21:48.500
I'm not going on TV again!

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:49.830
It's okay.

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:52.340
I stopped doing those documentaries.

00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:56.690
So I want to do a new project 
with you as the star.

00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:00.460
It's called "Bokuden's Explorers!"

00:22:00.780 --> 00:22:03.370
Our first episode will be "Kappa!"

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:11.970
<b>Bokuden's Explorers</b>

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:11.970
<b>Episode 1</b>

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:11.970
<b>The Kappa that Hide 
in the Mountain Rivers</b>

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:07.830
We'll go look for Kappa that
 hide in the mountain rivers!

00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:08.860
I'll go!

00:22:08.860 --> 00:22:10.970
I wanna find Kappa!

00:23:45.790 --> 00:23:48.530
Of course, the star of the next 
episode is still Bokuden, right?

00:23:48.530 --> 00:23:49.740
What? It's not?

00:23:49.740 --> 00:23:52.700
Next time it's somebody called 
Hiraga Gennai, the intellectual?

00:23:52.700 --> 00:23:55.590
Next time on Sengoku Collection: 
"Talented Master."

00:23:55.590 --> 00:23:57.400
She uses electricity attacks?

00:23:57.400 --> 00:23:59.700
I wonder if I could block 
it with a pot lid?
